# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the libFuzzer harnesses (fuzz workflow,
# Linux). Keep this list to allocations LeakSanitizer cannot trace, so any
# other per-input leak still fails the run.
#
# swift-corelibs-foundation's NSRegularExpression: LSan reports the ICU
# regex that _CFRegularExpressionCreate allocates as a direct leak even
# while the owning object is alive (seen for rv-fuzz-normalize's global
# `gate`, whose compiled packs live for the process, and for Foundation's
# own pattern cache behind `replacingOccurrences(options: .regularExpression)`).
# rv compiles only constant patterns, so these are one-time allocations.
leak:_CFRegularExpressionCreate
